a1 sets and elements · 集合与元素 for each of the following collection of items, determine if it is a set or not. if it is not a set, write down a set containing those elements.
a. $1,2,3,4$;
b. $\{1,2,4,3,3\}$;
c. $\{1,\{2,3\},4\}$;
d. $\varnothing$;
e. $\{\mathrm{blue},\mathrm{house}\}$;
f. $\{\mathrm{horse},\mathrm{cat},\varnothing\}$. 判断下列每组对象是否写成了集合；若不是，写出包含这些元素的集合。
a. $1,2,3,4$；
b. $\{1,2,4,3,3\}$；
c. $\{1,\{2,3\},4\}$；
d. $\varnothing$；
e. $\{\mathrm{blue},\mathrm{house}\}$；
f. $\{\mathrm{horse},\mathrm{cat},\varnothing\}$。 decide whether each item is written as a set. if not, put the listed objects into a set. the main skill is reading the braces correctly, not doing a calculation. 判断每一项是否写成了集合；若不是，把所列对象写成集合。重点不是计算，而是正确读出花括号的层次。 a set is a collection of distinct objects; order and repetition do not change the set. 集合由不同对象组成；元素顺序和重复书写不改变集合。 an element may itself be a set. $\varnothing$ is the set with no elements. 元素本身可以是集合。$\varnothing$ 是没有元素的集合。 look for the outside braces first. treat each complete object between them as one element, even if that object has its own braces. 先找最外层花括号，把其中每个完整对象当作一个元素；即使对象自己还有花括号，也先不拆开。 cross out repeated names only when counting distinct elements. writing the same object twice does not create a second copy in a set. 数不同元素时才忽略重复书写；同一个对象写两遍，不会在集合里变成两个元素。 check the empty set separately. having no elements does not stop it being a set; putting it inside another pair of braces creates a set with one element. 单独检查空集：没有元素并不妨碍它是集合；在它外面再加一对花括号，则得到一个只有一个元素的集合。 a. not a set as written in this notation exercise: add braces to obtain $\{1,2,3,4\}$. a. 按本题的记法要求，原式只列出了对象，未写成集合；补上花括号得 $\{1,2,3,4\}$。 b. yes. $\{1,2,4,3,3\}=\{1,2,3,4\}$, with four distinct elements. b. 是。$\{1,2,4,3,3\}=\{1,2,3,4\}$，有四个不同元素。重复的 3 不计两次。 c. yes. its three elements are $1$, the entire set $\{2,3\}$, and $4$. the number $2$ is not an element of the outer set. c. 是。三个元素分别是 $1$、整个集合 $\{2,3\}$、$4$。数字 $2$ 不是这个外层集合的元素。 d. yes. the empty set is a set, with zero elements. d. 是。空集也是集合，元素个数为零。 e. yes. the objects named blue and house can be elements; elements need not be numbers. e. 是。blue 和 house 在这里是对象名称；元素不必是数字。 f. yes. it has three elements: horse, cat, and the empty set. here the empty set counts as one object. f. 是。三个元素是 horse、cat、空集。空集在外层集合里作为一个完整对象，算一个元素。 check: $\varnothing\ne\{\varnothing\}$. the first has zero elements; the second has one. 检查理解：$\varnothing\ne\{\varnothing\}$。前者零个元素，后者一个元素。 count the objects at the outermost level. a set can itself be one of those objects. what changes if i put braces around the empty set? 数最外层的对象，集合本身也可以是其中一个对象。如果我在空集外加一对花括号，会发生什么变化？ do not reject a set because an element is repeated; repetition is simply ignored. 不要因为元素重复出现就说不是集合；重复书写只需忽略。 do not flatten nested braces: being inside an element is not the same as being an element of the outer set. 不要把嵌套括号摊平；出现在某个元素内部，不等于属于最外层集合。

a2 statements · 命题与表达式 which of the following are statements?
a. $3=2$;
b. $3+2$;
c. $3\ge2$;
d. $3$ and $2$;
e. $\{4\}\subseteq\mathbb z$ and $4\ne2$;
f. $4\in\mathbb z$ or $4+2$;
g. $\mathbb z\cap\mathbb q$;
h. $\mathbb z\subseteq\mathbb q$;
i. $|5|$. 以下哪些是命题（可以判断真假的陈述）？
a. $3=2$；b. $3+2$；c. $3\ge2$；d. $3$ 且 $2$；
e. $\{4\}\subseteq\mathbb z$ 且 $4\ne2$；
f. $4\in\mathbb z$ 或 $4+2$；
g. $\mathbb z\cap\mathbb q$；h. $\mathbb z\subseteq\mathbb q$；i. $|5|$。 sort the items into statements and expressions. a statement says something that is true or false; an expression may just name a number or a set. you are not being asked to keep only the true items. 把各项分成命题与表达式。命题说了一件能判真假的事；表达式可能只是表示一个数或集合。本题不是让你只挑正确说法。 a statement has a definite truth value: true or false. a false statement is still a statement. 命题有确定的真值：真或假。假命题仍然是命题。 logical “and” and “or” combine statements. a number or a set expression alone is not a statement. 逻辑“且”“或”连接的是命题；单独的数字表达式或集合表达式不是命题。 ask, “what is this item claiming?” for $3=2$, the claim is clear even though it is wrong. for $3+2$, no claim has been made yet. 先问“这一项声称了什么？”$3=2$ 虽然错，却有明确断言；$3+2$ 还没有作出断言。 for an item joined by “and” or “or”, test each side first. both sides need to be statements before the connecting word produces a statement. 遇到“且”或“或”，先分别检查两边；两边都须是命题，连接后才构成命题。 write “statement” or “not a statement” first. only then, if useful, add whether the statement is true or false. this keeps the two questions separate. 先写“是命题”或“不是命题”，再按需要补充真假，避免混淆两种判断。 a. yes, false: $3=2$ makes a definite assertion. a. 是，且为假；$3=2$ 是一个明确的断言。 b. no: $3+2$ names a number but asserts nothing. b. 不是：$3+2$ 表示一个数，没有作出断言。 c. yes, true: $3\ge2$. c. 是，且为真：$3\ge2$。 d. no: neither $3$ nor $2$ is a statement to which logical “and” applies. d. 不是：$3$ 和 $2$ 本身都不是命题，不能这样用逻辑“且”连接。 e. yes, true: both $\{4\}\subseteq\mathbb z$ and $4\ne2$ are true statements. their conjunction, meaning the two joined by “and”, is therefore true. e. 是，且为真：$\{4\}\subseteq\mathbb z$ 和 $4\ne2$ 都是真命题。二者用“且”连接所得的命题（称为合取）也为真。 f. no: $4\in\mathbb z$ is a statement, but $4+2$ is not; “or” does not repair the missing assertion. f. 不是：前半是命题，但 $4+2$ 不是；加一个“或”不能使后半自动变成命题。 g. no: $\mathbb z\cap\mathbb q$ denotes a set. g. 不是：$\mathbb z\cap\mathbb q$ 表示集合，而非关于集合的陈述。 h. yes, true: every integer is rational, since $n=n/1$. h. 是，且为真：每个整数都是有理数，因为 $n=n/1$。 i. no: $|5|$ denotes the number $5$. for comparison, $|5|\ge6$ is a statement, although false. the complete answer is a, c, e and h. i. 不是：$|5|$ 表示数 $5$。改成 $|5|\ge6$ 就是命题，虽然是假命题。完整答案为 a、c、e、h。 we are not asking whether each item is true. we are asking whether it is the kind of sentence that can be true or false. 我们不是在问每项是否正确，而是在问它是不是一种能够判真假的句子。 do not confuse “is a statement” with “is a true statement”. 不要混淆“是命题”和“是真命题”。 an expression with a calculable value still need not assert anything. 表达式能够算出值，不代表它作出了可判断真假的断言。

a3 membership versus subset · 元素与子集 let $a=\{\mathrm{cat},\{1,\mathrm{cat}\},\alpha,\{\alpha\}\}$. which of the following statements are true?
a. $\mathrm{cat}\in a$;
b. $\{\mathrm{cat}\}\notin a$;
c. $\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}\subseteq a$;
d. $\{\mathrm{cat},\alpha\}\subseteq a$;
e. $\varnothing\subsetneq a$;
f. $a=\{\alpha,\mathrm{cat},\{1,\mathrm{cat}\},\{\alpha\}\}$;
g. $a=\{1,\{1,\mathrm{cat}\},\alpha\}$. 令 $a=\{\mathrm{cat},\{1,\mathrm{cat}\},\alpha,\{\alpha\}\}$。判断以下命题哪些为真。
a. $\mathrm{cat}\in a$；b. $\{\mathrm{cat}\}\notin a$；
c. $\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}\subseteq a$；d. $\{\mathrm{cat},\alpha\}\subseteq a$；
e. $\varnothing\subsetneq a$；
f. $a=\{\alpha,\mathrm{cat},\{1,\mathrm{cat}\},\{\alpha\}\}$；
g. $a=\{1,\{1,\mathrm{cat}\},\alpha\}$。 use one fixed set to test three different ideas: being an element, being a subset, and being equal to another set. for each line, choose the test that matches its symbol. 围绕同一个集合检查三件不同的事：属于、是子集、集合相等。每一行先看符号，再选对应的检验方法。 $u\in a$ asks whether the entire object $u$ is one of the elements of $a$. $s\subseteq a$ asks whether every element of $s$ belongs to $a$. $u\in a$ 问整个对象 $u$ 是否是 $a$ 的一个元素；$s\subseteq a$ 问 $s$ 的每个元素是否都属于 $a$。 $s\subsetneq a$ means $s\subseteq a$ and $s\ne a$. two sets are equal exactly when they have the same elements. $s\subsetneq a$ 表示 $s\subseteq a$ 且 $s\ne a$。集合相等当且仅当元素完全相同。 list the four outer-level elements of $a$ before judging any line. keep each inner set together as a complete object. this stops the hidden $1$ from being mistaken for an element of $a$. 判断前先列出 a 最外层的四个元素。内部集合要整体保留，避免把藏在内层的 1 错认成 a 的元素。 for $u\in a$, compare the whole $u$ with that list. for $s\subseteq a$, open $s$ and check its elements one at a time. one missing element is enough to make a subset claim false. 判断 $u\in a$ 时，把整个 u 与列表比较；判断 $s\subseteq a$ 时，打开 s，逐一检查它的元素。只要找到一个不在 a 中的元素，子集关系就不成立。 for a proper subset, also check that the sets are not equal. for equality, compare the elements rather than their order. finally, read “not in” carefully: a true answer may mean that something is absent. 真子集还要检查不相等；相等则比较元素，不比较顺序。最后注意“不属于”的否定号：答案为真可能正是在说某个对象不在里面。 first identify the four outer-level elements: $\mathrm{cat}$, $\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}$, $\alpha$, $\{\alpha\}$. 先识别最外层四个元素：$\mathrm{cat}$、$\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}$、$\alpha$、$\{\alpha\}$。 a. true: $\mathrm{cat}$ is explicitly an element of $a$. a. 真：$\mathrm{cat}$ 直接列为 $a$ 的元素。 b. true: the entire singleton $\{\mathrm{cat}\}$ is not an element of $a$. do not confuse it with $\mathrm{cat}$. b. 真：整个单元素集合 $\{\mathrm{cat}\}$ 不属于 $a$；它与 $\mathrm{cat}$ 是不同对象。 c. false: $1\in\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}$ but $1\notin a$. this one counterexample disproves the subset claim. nevertheless, $\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}\in a$ is true. c. 假：$1\in\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}$，但 $1\notin a$。一个反例就能否定子集关系。不过 $\{1,\mathrm{cat}\}\in a$ 确实为真。 d. true: both elements of the left-hand set, $\mathrm{cat}$ and $\alpha$, belong to $a$. d. 真：左侧集合的每个元素，即 $\mathrm{cat}$ 与 $\alpha$，都属于 $a$。 e. true: the empty set is a subset of every set, and here $a\ne\varnothing$, so the inclusion is strict. e. 真：空集是任何集合的子集，且这里 $a$ 非空，所以是严格子集。 f. true: the same four elements are simply written in a different order. f. 真：只调换了同样四个元素的书写顺序。 g. false: $\{\alpha\}$ is missing from the right-hand side. also $\mathrm{cat}$ is missing as an outer-level element, and $1$ has been added. g. 假：右边缺少元素 $\{\alpha\}$；也缺少作为外层元素的 $\mathrm{cat}$，并多了 $1$。 the answer sequence is t, t, f, t, t, t, f. transfer check: both $\{\alpha\}\in a$ and $\{\alpha\}\subseteq a$ are true, for different reasons. 答案顺序为真、真、假、真、真、真、假。迁移检查：$\{\alpha\}\in a$ 与 $\{\alpha\}\subseteq a$ 都为真，但理由不同。 for membership, keep the object on the left intact. for a subset, check every element of the set on the left. can you find one element that makes part c fail? 检查属于时，把左侧整个对象保留不拆；检查子集时，逐个检查左侧集合的元素。你能找出使 c 失败的那个元素吗？ $\in$ and $\subseteq$ are different tests. neither implies the other in general. $\in$ 和 $\subseteq$ 是不同检验，一般不能由其中一个推出另一个。 the empty set is always a subset, but is not automatically an element. a proper subset also requires inequality. 空集总是子集，但不自动成为元素。严格子集还要求两集合不相等。

a8 indexed unions and intersections · 集合族 let $\{a_i:i\in\mathbb z_{\ge0}\}$ be a collection of subsets of $\mathbb z$ defined by $a_i=\{x\in\mathbb z:-i\le x\le i\}$. find:
a. $\displaystyle\bigcup_{i\in\{1,2,3,4\}}a_i$;
b. $\displaystyle\bigcap_{i\in\{1,2,3,4\}}a_i$;
c. $\displaystyle\bigcup_{i\in\mathbb z_{\ge0}}a_i$;
d. $\displaystyle\bigcap_{i\in\mathbb z_{\ge0}}a_i$. 对非负整数 i，定义整数子集 $a_i=\{x\in\mathbb z:-i\le x\le i\}$。求：
a. $\displaystyle\bigcup_{i\in\{1,2,3,4\}}a_i$；
b. $\displaystyle\bigcap_{i\in\{1,2,3,4\}}a_i$；
c. $\displaystyle\bigcup_{i\in\mathbb z_{\ge0}}a_i$；
d. $\displaystyle\bigcap_{i\in\mathbb z_{\ge0}}a_i$。 the sets get wider as the index increases. find which integers appear in at least one selected set, or remain in every selected set. read the index range carefully: some parts include a0 and others do not. 下标越大，集合越宽。并集找至少在某个指定集合里的整数；交集找每个指定集合里都有的整数。特别注意有的小问含 a0，有的从 a1 开始。 a union contains elements in at least one indexed set; an intersection contains elements in every indexed set. 属于集合族的并集，指至少属于其中一个；属于交集，指属于其中每一个。 for nested finite sets, the union is the largest and the intersection the smallest of the sets actually indexed. 有限嵌套集合的并取实际参与运算的最大者，交取最小者。 write out a0, a1 and a2 first. you will see that each set contains the one before it, so the sets fit inside each other. 先列 a0、a1、a2，就能看出每个集合都包含前一个，形成一层套一层的关系。 for the four-set questions, use that pattern. the largest selected set contains everything the union can contain; the smallest selected set contains exactly what all four share. 只涉及四个集合时利用这个规律：最大的已包含并集的全部元素，最小的恰好留下四者共有的元素。 for the infinite union, there is no largest index. instead, start with any integer n and choose an index large enough to include it. taking the absolute value of n works even when n is negative. 无限并没有最大的下标。改为任取整数 n，再选一个足够大的下标把它包含进去。取 n 的绝对值，负整数也同样适用。 for the infinite intersection, ask what is left after requiring membership in a0 as well as every other set. then check that the remaining candidate really belongs to all of them. 无限交还要求属于 a0，先看这一要求留下什么，再确认剩下的候选元素确实属于所有其他集合。 list the first sets: $a_0=\{0\}$, $a_1=\{-1,0,1\}$, $a_2=\{-2,-1,0,1,2\}$. thus $a_0\subseteq a_1\subseteq a_2\subseteq\cdots$. 先列 $a_0=\{0\}$、$a_1=\{-1,0,1\}$、$a_2=\{-2,-1,0,1,2\}$，可见集合逐渐扩大。 a. the largest of $a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4$ is $a_4$, so the union is $\{-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4\}$. a. 四个集合中 $a_4$ 最大，所以并集为 $\{-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4\}$。 b. their smallest set is $a_1$, so the intersection is $\{-1,0,1\}$. b. 四个集合中 $a_1$ 最小，所以交集为 $\{-1,0,1\}$。 c. every $a_i$ contains only integers, so the union is a subset of $\mathbb z$. conversely, given any $n\in\mathbb z$, take $i=|n|$; then $n\in a_{|n|}$. hence the union equals $\mathbb z$. c. 每个 $a_i$ 只含整数，所以并集包含于整数集合。反过来，任取整数 n，选非负整数下标 $i=|n|$，则 $n\in a_{|n|}$。两个方向合起来，并集为全体整数。 d. zero lies in every $a_i$. any element of the intersection must in particular lie in $a_0=\{0\}$. therefore the intersection is exactly $\{0\}$. d. 零属于每个 $a_i$；交集中的元素又必须属于 $a_0=\{0\}$，所以交集恰为 $\{0\}$。 before calculating, list the first few sets and check the index range. in part c there is no largest index, so explain how any chosen integer gets included. 先列前几个集合，并看清下标范围。c 不存在最大的下标，要解释任意给定整数怎样被包含进去。 parts a and b start at 1; parts c and d include 0. this changes the smallest set. a、b 从 1 开始；c、d 包含下标 0，因此最小集合不同。 do not describe the infinite union as the largest $a_i$: no such $a_i$ exists. 不要说无限并等于最大的 $a_i$；这里不存在这样的最大成员。
